.\" man page for mos (mac-optical-state)
.\" Source of truth for the grammar is cli/main.c (usage) and include/mos.h
.\" (states, exit codes). Keep this file in sync with both when the surface
.\" changes; the CLI contract test (tests/cli/test_cli.sh) pins the behavior.
.TH MOS 1 "2026-06-18" "mac-optical-state" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mos \- report the state of a macOS optical drive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mos
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ drive ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mos
.I drive
.RI "(bare selector runs " state )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mos
reports what a macOS optical drive is actually doing \(em tray open, tray
closed on an empty slot, loading, unit ready, busy \(em by querying the drive
directly over MMC. Unlike
.BR drutil (1),
which prints
.I No Media Inserted
for both an open tray and a closed-but-empty one,
.B mos
distinguishes them.
.PP
A state query costs at most two MMC commands (TEST UNIT READY plus a tray
probe or profile read). It needs no entitlements and no root \(em only the
console user's SCSITaskUserClient grant on the drive.
.PP
.B mos
is also an embeddable pure-C library; see
.B mos.h
and the project documentation.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BR state " [" \fIdrive\fR ]
Report drive state. This is the default verb: a bare drive selector
.RB ( "mos 2" ", " "mos disk4" )
runs it without the verb word. Emits
.IR mos.state.v1 .
.TP
.B list
List all drives with their states. Emits
.IR mos.list.v1 .
.TP
.BR watch " [" \fIdrive\fR ]
Stream state events as newline-delimited JSON
.RI ( mos.event.v1 )
until SIGINT. Watches all drives unless a drive narrows it; hot-plugged
drives join the stream and a removed drive does not end it.
.B \-\-json
is a no-op here (watch is always NDJSON).
.TP
.BR metadata " [" \fIdrive\fR ]
Disc identity record \(em profile, TOC, disc info, mounted volume. Emits
.IR mos.metadata.v1 .
.TP
.BR drive " [" \fIdrive\fR ]
Drive facts \(em identity, serial, content protection, firmware date. Emits
.IR mos.drive.v1 .
.TP
.BR features " [" \fIdrive\fR ]
MMC feature list with current bits (the medium-writability surface). Emits
.IR mos.features.v1 .
.TP
.BR tray " \fIaction\fR [" \fIdrive\fR ]
Control the tray. \fIaction\fR is one of
.BR eject ", " close ", " lock ", or " unlock .
.B eject
takes
.BR \-\-force
(issue an ALLOW first, so a basic lock does not block the eject);
.B lock
and
.B unlock
take
.BR \-\-persistent
(the Persistent Prevent state, which converts the operator eject button
into an event rather than ejecting). Emits
.IR mos.tray.v1 .
A refusal (for example, an eject hitting a lock) is a reported outcome,
not an error.
.TP
.BR capacity " [" \fIdrive\fR ]
Disc capacity \(em media size plus the recordable free / append space. Emits
.IR mos.capacity.v1 .
.TP
.BR probe " \fIdrive\fR"
Diagnostic. Streams raw IOKit / DiscRecording notification events as NDJSON
.RI ( mos.probe.v0 )
until SIGINT; with
.BR \-\-dump ,
a one-shot DiscRecording Info/Status plist capture (takes no drive
argument). Present only when the binary was built with
.BR \-DMOS_CLI_PROBE=ON " (the default)."
.SH DRIVE SELECTOR
The
.I drive
is a positional argument, like
.BR "diskutil info disk4" .
With a single drive attached it may be omitted; with several it is
required. Three forms:
.TP
.B Index
A 1-based index from the
.B Index
column of
.BR "mos list" ;
all digits (for example,
.BR 1 ).
Positional and not durable \(em it races device hot-plug. Use it only for
one-shot, human-driven invocations.
.TP
.B registry_id
The drive's attachment identity, as printed in the
.B Registry ID:
row or the JSON
.B registry_id
field; all digits, at or above 2^32. Never reused; stable for the life of
an attachment.
.TP
.B BSD form
.BR disk4 ", " rdisk4 ", or " /dev/disk4 .
.PP
.RB ( probe
accepts an index or BSD form only, no registry_id.)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-index " \fIN\fR"
1-based drive index; the explicit form of the positional Index selector.
.TP
.BR \-\-bsd " \fINAME\fR"
BSD form; the explicit form of the positional BSD selector.
.TP
.B \-\-force
With
.BR "tray eject" :
issue an ALLOW (unlock) before ejecting.
.TP
.B \-\-persistent
With
.BR "tray lock" " / " "tray unlock" :
select the Persistent Prevent state.
.TP
.B \-\-dump
With
.BR probe :
one-shot DiscRecording dictionary capture (text + XML plists; takes no
drive argument).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Emit JSON
.RI ( mos.state.v1 " / " mos.error.v1 " / " mos.list.v1 ).
Takes no argument \(em each schema name carries its own version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
These apply to
.B watch
only. Each is an integer number of milliseconds in the range
0..3600000, where 0 selects the library default; an out-of-range or
non-numeric value warns on stderr and falls back to the default.
.TP
.B MOS_WATCH_STABLE_MS
Poll period in stable states (default 2000).
.TP
.B MOS_WATCH_TRANSITION_MS
Poll period in transitional states (default 200).
.SH STATES
.BR open ", " empty ", " loading ", " ready ", " busy ", " formatting ", "
.BR media_unreadable ", " device_fault ", " empty_or_open ", " unknown .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B mos
uses
.BR sysexits.h (3)
codes:
.TP
.B 0
A drive state was observed (including
.BR unknown ,
which is a valid result).
.TP
.B 64
Usage error
.RB ( EX_USAGE ).
.TP
.B 66
No such device
.RB ( EX_NOINPUT ).
.TP
.B 69
Unavailable \(em driver rejected or command unsupported
.RB ( EX_UNAVAILABLE ).
.TP
.B 70
Internal error
.RB ( EX_SOFTWARE ).
.TP
.B 71
OS error
.RB ( EX_OSERR ).
.TP
.B 74
I/O error
.RB ( EX_IOERR ).
.TP
.B 75
Temporary failure \(em busy, contended, or timed out
.RB ( EX_TEMPFAIL ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Report the state of the only attached drive:
.B mos state
.TP
Report drive 1 as JSON:
.B mos state 1 \-\-json
.TP
List every drive:
.B mos list
.TP
Act on each disc that becomes readable, hot-plug included:
.B mos watch | jq ...
.TP
Eject drive 1, unlocking first if needed:
.B mos tray eject 1 \-\-force
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR drutil (1),
.BR diskutil (8),
.BR sysexits (3)
.PP
